13d:["$","p","p-100",{"children":"Inspect resources before deleting the namespace:"}]
13e:["$","pre","pre-64",{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-bash","children":"kubectl -n shopsmart get all\n"}]}]
13f:["$","p","p-101",{"children":"When you are sure this is a disposable project namespace:"}]
140:["$","pre","pre-65",{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-bash","children":"kubectl delete namespace shopsmart\n"}]}]
141:["$","p","p-102",{"children":"If you installed Argo CD solely for this project and do not need it for other apps:"}]
142:["$","pre","pre-66",{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-bash","children":"kubectl delete namespace argocd\n"}]}]
143:["$","p","p-103",{"children":"Delete the local cluster only if you no longer need it."}]
144:["$","p","p-104",{"children":"For kind:"}]
145:["$","pre","pre-67",{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-bash","children":"kind delete cluster --name shopsmart\n"}]}]
146:["$","p","p-105",{"children":"For minikube:"}]
147:["$","pre","pre-68",{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-bash","children":"minikube delete\n"}]}]
148:["$","p","p-106",{"children":"These commands are destructive to the specified local cluster/namespace. Confirm the active context and the resources first."}]
149:["$","hr","hr-25",{}]
14a:["$","h2","h2-25",{"children":"🎤 Interview Preparation"}]
14b:["$","h3","h3-59",{"children":"1. What is Kubernetes?"}]
14c:["$","p","p-107",{"children":"Kubernetes is a container orchestration platform. It manages deployment, scheduling, service discovery, scaling, and recovery of containerized workloads."}]
14d:["$","h3","h3-60",{"children":"2. What is the difference between a Pod and a Deployment?"}]
14e:["$","p","p-108",{"children":"A Pod is the smallest deployable unit. A Deployment declares the desired replica count and Pod template, and manages ReplicaSets to support rollout and replacement."}]
14f:["$","h3","h3-61",{"children":"3. What is a Service?"}]
150:["$","p","p-109",{"children":"A Service gives a stable network endpoint to a group of Pods selected by labels. It avoids depending on individual Pod IP addresses."}]
151:["$","h3","h3-62",{"children":"4. What is Helm?"}]
152:["$","p","p-110",{"children":"Helm is a Kubernetes package manager. A chart contains templates and default values that can be configured for different environments and releases."}]
153:["$","h3","h3-63",{"children":"5. What is GitOps?"}]
154:["$","p","p-111",{"children":"GitOps is an operational approach in which a version-controlled repository describes the desired system state. A controller compares that state with the live system and reconciles differences."}]
155:["$","h3","h3-64",{"children":"6. What is Argo CD?"}]
156:["$","p","p-112",{"children":"Argo CD is a declarative GitOps continuous delivery tool for Kubernetes. It monitors configured sources and applications, shows sync/health status, and can reconcile resources according to its policies."}]
157:["$","h3","h3-65",{"children":"7. What is the difference between CI and GitOps CD?"}]
158:["$","p","p-113",{"children":"CI normally builds and tests code, and may publish an image. GitOps CD applies the declared deployment configuration from Git to the cluster. They are complementary but separate responsibilities."}]
159:["$","h3","h3-66",{"children":"8. What is the difference between readiness and liveness probes?"}]
15a:["$","p","p-114",{"children":"Readiness determines whether a Pod should receive normal Service traffic. Liveness detects a container that should be restarted. Startup probes give applications extra time to initialize."}]
15b:["$","h3","h3-67",{"children":["9. What is ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"ImagePullBackOff"}],"?"]}]
15c:["$","p","p-115",{"children":"It indicates Kubernetes is having trouble retrieving the requested image. Common causes include an incorrect image/tag, registry access problems, missing credentials, or an image not being available to the node."}]
15d:["$","h3","h3-68",{"children":"10. What is configuration drift?"}]
15e:["$","p","p-116",{"children":"Drift occurs when live resources differ from the declared desired state. GitOps tools can detect it and, when configured, reconcile it."}]
15f:["$","h3","h3-69",{"children":"11. How do you roll back a failed GitOps deployment?"}]
160:["$","p","p-117",{"children":"I identify the failing version and symptoms, revert the deployment configuration or image reference in Git, push the change, let Argo CD reconcile, and verify Pod readiness and application behaviour."}]
161:["$","h3","h3-70",{"children":"12. Why are resource requests and limits useful?"}]
162:["$","p","p-118",{"children":"Requests help the scheduler decide where a Pod can run. Limits constrain resource consumption for supported resources and help protect the cluster, though poor values can cause throttling or out-of-memory terminations."}]
163:["$","h3","h3-71",{"children":"13. Does creating an Ingress resource expose the app automatically?"}]
164:["$","p","p-119",{"children":"No. An Ingress resource defines routing rules; a compatible Ingress controller must be installed and configured, and DNS/networking must point traffic appropriately."}]
165:["$","h3","h3-72",{"children":"14. Why should production deployment images use immutable versions?"}]
166:["$","p","p-120",{"children":"Immutable tags or image digests make the deployed artifact identifiable and reduce uncertainty caused by a tag being changed to point to different image content."}]
167:["$","h3","h3-73",{"children":"15. How would you improve this project for production?"}]
168:["$","p","p-121",{"children":"I would add a managed cluster, private networking, RBAC, network policies, TLS, secret management, image scanning/signing, environment promotion, policy checks, monitoring/alerts, backup/recovery planning, and documented operational procedures."}]
169:["$","h3","h3-74",{"children":"Sample interview explanation"}]
16a:["$","blockquote","blockquote-4",{"children":["\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":"“I built a Kubernetes GitOps learning project for a sample product API. I containerized the application with Docker, deployed it with Kubernetes Deployments and Services, and packaged the resources using Helm. I configured Argo CD to track a Git repository and reconcile the desired state into the cluster. I validated health probes, rollout behaviour, image-pull failures, and drift recovery, and documented monitoring and security improvements. The project was first tested on a local cluster; I would validate the cloud networking, access controls, and operational requirements separately before using it in production.”"}],"\n"]}]
16b:["$","p","p-122",{"children":"Only say you completed a stage if you actually implemented and tested it."}]
16c:["$","hr","hr-26",{}]
16d:["$","h2","h2-26",{"children":"📚 Official Documentation"}]
